cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Ungrounded: Entity Groundability Shifts Tool Routing in LLM Agents
message: If you use this software or data, please cite it as below.
type: software
version: 1.2.0
authors:
  - given-names: Taran
    family-names: Douley
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0002-3673-4500'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Taran-Douley/ungrounded-agents'
abstract: >-
  Harnesses, raw per-trial data and analysis for five studies
  (16,350 trials, six models, two vendors) showing that entity
  groundability shifts tool routing in LLM agents, and that
  supplying the missing argument removes the shift for named
  vendors. Also includes follow-up studies on tool order,
  reasoning effort, an entity-resolution guard, two-turn
  consequence, content-delivered entities and real MCP servers.
keywords:
  - LLM agents
  - tool use
  - tool routing
  - entity grounding
  - Model Context Protocol
  - agent evaluation
  - canary tokens
  - agent security
references:
  - type: software
    title: "ungrounded: an eval for LLM agent tool routing"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/Taran-Douley/ungrounded"
    url: "https://pypi.org/project/ungrounded/"
license: MIT
date-released: '2026-11-12'
